  "description": "YUHXUX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H73 Ce6 F1 N2 O31,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.706-3.823 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 114.91-119.43°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6O4(OH)3F(O2CPh)12(py)2]·MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
